# Opt-in private input and tracking debug views

Status: DONE
Milestone: M2 diagnostic UX
Dependencies: 03_BODY_FACE_TRACKING.todo, 05_STUDIO_AND_LAUNCH.todo

## Purpose
Provide the explicitly requested raw input window, skeleton-only black view and connected
face-landmark black view without leaking them into the avatar/clean output.

## Tasks
- [x] Add three separate default-off debug toggles/windows and close/reopen behavior.
- [x] Pair opt-in raw retention with processed observations; clear on disable/stop/staleness.
- [x] Draw measured skeleton and face connections on black with honest input-orientation labels.
- [x] Configure requested auth defaults only in ignored user-encrypted local storage.
- [x] Validate privacy/lifecycle/render behavior and maintain guides/journal/context.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] No debug pixels enter the main or clean output; raw preview is explicit and private.
- [x] No credentials are hard-coded, documented, logged or stored in context.
- [x] Missing/old inputs clear rather than inventing a detected skeleton/face.

